@lang en
-- Tests of ie-month-year-readings.l4: what each alternative reading WOULD answer. None of these is the Act's answer.
-- Expected values were worked out on a calendar before the code ran (the arithmetic of the corresponding date, and the days of a short month).
-- Each case is also set beside the Act's own answer, which is a refusal, so that the contrast is itself tested.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-month-year-readings`

§ `Reading B: the corresponding date, clamped (daydate add months / add years)`

-- the worked cases
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 3 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- more months
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 15
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 13 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2024 1 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2024 1 30) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2024 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `reading B: the corresponding date` 4 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
-- not a period
#ASSERT REFUSED `reading B: the corresponding date` 0 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `reading B: the corresponding date` 0 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 7 16)
-- first day included (the day before the corresponding date)
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 3 `years from` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 15
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 5 `years from` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 14
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 5 `years from` (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 8 31
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 2 `years from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 1 `years from` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 27
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 1 `calendar months from` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 27
#ASSERT `reading B, first day included: the last day of` 1 `calendar months from` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 14

§ `Reading C: the corresponding date, rolled forward when the month has no such day`

#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 3
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2024 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 2
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2024 1 30) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2024 1 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 3 31) EQUALS YMD 2025 5 1
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 15
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 4 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 3 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `reading C: the corresponding date` 5 `years after` (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `reading C: the corresponding date` 0 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"
-- readings B and C part company exactly where the month or year has no such day
#ASSERT NOT (`reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS (`reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `calendar months after` (YMD 2025 1 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`reading B: the corresponding date` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS (`reading C: the corresponding date` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29))
#ASSERT (`reading B: the corresponding date` 3 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16)) EQUALS (`reading C: the corresponding date` 3 `years after` (YMD 2025 7 16))

§ `Reading D: N weeks from any day is seven times N days`

#ASSERT `reading D: the last day of` 1 `weeks from any day` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 7
#ASSERT `reading D: the last day of` 2 `weeks from any day` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 14
-- from a Sunday it agrees with the Act
#ASSERT `reading D: the last day of` 1 `weeks from any day` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 10
#ASSERT `reading D: the last day of` 1 `weeks from any day` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 4)
-- the Act refuses where reading D answers
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `reading D: the last day of` 0 `weeks from any day` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"

§ `The Act refuses where readings B and C answer: the contrast, for each worked case`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 3 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 5 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 15)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 5 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 2 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 28)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 31)

§ `Reading R: a last day on a day of rest rolls forward (rest days here are Saturday, Sunday and the two holidays below)`

`holidays supplied by the tests` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD elem d (LIST (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 1 5))

`days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD (NOT `is weekday` d) OR `holidays supplied by the tests` d

-- Friday: stays
#ASSERT `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (YMD 2026 1 2) `, rest days being` `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` `, searching` 10 `days at most` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
-- Thursday (a holiday): Friday
#ASSERT `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, rest days being` `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` `, searching` 10 `days at most` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
-- Saturday: Sunday, then Monday (a holiday), so Tuesday
#ASSERT `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (YMD 2026 1 3) `, rest days being` `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` `, searching` 10 `days at most` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
-- Sunday: the same Tuesday
#ASSERT `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (YMD 2026 1 4) `, rest days being` `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` `, searching` 10 `days at most` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
-- search limit boundary: from Saturday, four days reach Tuesday; three do not
#ASSERT `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (YMD 2026 1 3) `, rest days being` `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` `, searching` 4 `days at most` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
#ASSERT REFUSED `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (YMD 2026 1 3) `, rest days being` `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` `, searching` 3 `days at most` BECAUSE "no day was found within the search limit"
-- the Act refuses on the same Saturday
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 3) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests`
